You have failed. The price must be paid.	你已然失敗。這代價，終須償還。
When light is dim and courage fails, When heart against adversity rails, When it seems you will never see the dawn, This alone can drive you on.	當光線黯淡、勇氣潰散之時，當心因逆境而痛楚難平之時，當你彷彿再難見到黎明之時，唯獨此物，能催你向前。
If a dream is abandoned, Or a purpose dies, These are left with the dregs Of bitterness and sighs.	若夢想遭到棄置，或志向就此消亡，殘留下來的，唯有苦澀與嘆息的渣滓。
It can be sweet on the tongue, Or vile as a curse, To hear it is evil, To believe it is worse.	它可以在舌尖上甘甜，也可以惡毒如詛咒，聽聞它是邪惡之事，相信它則更加不堪。
In time of grief, It gives relief, It can lessen fears, Ease the pain of tears.	在悲傷之際，它帶來寬慰，能減輕恐懼，撫平淚水的傷痛。
Oh, it is splendid, It has no peer, It scorns the lesser, And holds itself dear.	噢，它輝煌燦爛，舉世無雙，它蔑視卑微之物，唯獨珍視自身。
Known to the priest And nun, Who natural pleasures Do shun.	為僧侶與修女所熟知，儘管他們棄絕世俗的歡愉。
Surrounded by giants, Your worries were few, Wonders abounded, The world was new.	身邊環繞著巨人，你的煩憂寥寥無幾，奇蹟俯拾皆是，世界猶然嶄新。
Wise are they who seek it, Fools are they who believe without it, Scorn those who claim To own it.	尋求它的人是智者，不憑它便輕信的人是愚者，聲稱擁有它的人，該受人鄙夷。
It alleviates all pain and sorrows, The final end of all tomorrows, That to which we all must go, Rich or poor, high or low.	它能消解一切苦痛與哀傷，是所有明日終將抵達的盡頭，是無論貧富貴賤，眾人終須奔赴之處。
For its sweet sake, You suffer in silence, What we both most desire, But will never possess.	為了它的甜美，你默默承受痛苦，那是我們彼此最渴望，卻永遠無法擁有之物。
I need a bit more, m'lud, if you wish to go to the port you have chosen.	還需要再多一些，吾王，方能前往您所選定的港口。
Beggin' m'lud's pardon, but this is not enough for the port you have chosen.  I will return your coins, so you may count them out again.	請吾王恕罪，這些銀錢不夠前往您所選的港口。容小人將錢幣奉還，請您重新點過。
That is too much money, m'lud.  I cannot in all honesty accept more than is needed.	這錢太多了，吾王。憑良心，小人不能收下超出所需的部分。
Thankee, m'lud.  You have booked passage to Gaza.	多謝，吾王。您已訂下前往加薩的船位。
Thankee, m'lud.  You have booked passage to Thessalonica.	多謝，吾王。您已訂下前往帖撒羅尼迦的船位。
Thankee, m'lud.  You have booked passage to Rome.	多謝，吾王。您已訂下前往羅馬的船位。
Thankee, m'lud.  You have booked passage to Rennes.	多謝，吾王。您已訂下前往勒恩的船位。
Thankee, m'lud.  You have booked passage to Dublin.	多謝，吾王。您已訂下前往都柏林的船位。
He has the rolling gait of a retired sailor, and the portly bearing of a man who well enjoys his food and grog.	他走起路來步履搖晃，是退役水手的姿態，一身豐腴則透著愛好美食與烈酒之人的氣派。
'Tis a foreign ship, m'lud, recently sold to yet another foreigner.	這是一艘外國船，吾王，近日才又賣給了另一個外邦人。
There are many ships that use this port, m'lud, like the foreign ship behind me that arrived a few days ago.	有許多船隻使用這個港口，吾王，就像我身後那艘幾天前才抵達的外國船。
The "Conal Cearnach" sails for Dublin, m'lud, in the land of Eire. The "Frastrada" will dock somewhere along the coast of Brittany to deliver supplies for the scholars of Rennes in the Kingdom of the Franks.	「Conal Cearnach」號啟航前往愛爾蘭之地的都柏林，吾王。「Frastrada」號則會停靠布列塔尼沿岸某處，為法蘭克王國勒恩的學者們運送補給。
The Captain of the "Remus" seeks to reach Rome, but will stop in two Muslim-held ports, Malaga and Tunis.  The "Athene" sails for Thessalonica, seeking also to trade in Malaga and Tunis.	「Remus」號的船長意欲抵達羅馬，但途中會停靠穆斯林治下的馬拉加與突尼斯兩港。「Athene」號則駛往帖撒羅尼迦，同樣打算在馬拉加與突尼斯進行貿易。
A ship called "Al-Uzza" is bound for the Far East, by way of Malaga, Tunis, and Alexandria, and if God wills, coming at last to distant Gaza.	一艘名叫「Al-Uzza」的船正駛向遠東，途經馬拉加、突尼斯與亞歷山卓，若上天垂憐，終將抵達遙遠的加薩。
If you care to book passage on any of these, m'lud, I will gladly help you.	若吾王有意訂下其中任一艘的船位，小人樂意效勞。
I bid you to return later, m'lud, when the ships may be ready to sail.	還請吾王稍後再來，待船隻備妥啟航之時。
No need to part with it, m'lud.  Being small, it should fit on a ship well enough.	不必捨棄它，吾王。它體積不大，船上盡夠容納。
I know little about mules, m'lud.	小人對騾子所知不多，吾王。
 Beg pardon, m'lud?	 您說什麼，吾王？
There will not be enough room for your horse, m'lud.	空間不夠容納您的坐騎，吾王。
Aye, 'tis a fine horse.	正是，這是匹良駒。
Beg pardon, m'lud?	您說什麼，吾王？
The fare to Dublin is one silver coin. The fare to Rennes is two silver coins. The fare to Rome is one gold coin. The fare to Thessalonica is two gold coins. The fare to Gaza is three gold coins.	前往都柏林的船費是一枚銀幣。前往勒恩的船費是兩枚銀幣。前往羅馬的船費是一枚金幣。前往帖撒羅尼迦的船費是兩枚金幣。前往加薩的船費是三枚金幣。
I stand ready to accept your fare, m'lud, upon which I shall direct you to the proper ship.	小人已備妥收取吾王的船費，收訖之後便為您指引正確的船隻。
Please return later, m'lud, when ships are ready to sail.  Then I will be able to help you book passage.	請吾王稍後再來，待船隻備妥啟航，屆時小人便能為您訂下船位。
Jerusalem is a city in the desert near the easternmost end of the Mediterranean Sea.	耶路撒冷是一座位於沙漠中的城市，靠近地中海的最東端。
Eh? Sounds like some foreign word to me.	嗯？聽起來像是某個外邦詞語。
I know nothing of such things.	此事小人一概不知。
Of these good knights, I have heard no tale.	這幾位騎士的事，小人未曾聽聞。
Aye, he took ship from here to the Far East.  He said he had heard tales that made him believe he should seek the Grail in Jerusalem.	正是，他從此地搭船前往遠東。他說他聽聞的種種傳言，讓他相信該到耶路撒冷尋找聖杯。
There be five ships in port today, m'lud.  They are called the Conal Cearnach, the Frastrada, the Al-Uzza, the Athene and the Remus.	今日港中共有五艘船，吾王。它們分別喚作 Conal Cearnach、Frastrada、Al-Uzza、Athene 與 Remus。
My name is Rollin' Jack, m'lud.	小人名叫搖擺傑克，吾王。
Aye, m'lud, it were a hard life what does it to a man.	正是，吾王，這行當著實艱苦，磨人得很。
The "Conal Cearnach" sails for Dublin, m'lud, in the land of Eire.	「Conal Cearnach」號啟航前往愛爾蘭之地的都柏林，吾王。
The "Frastrada" will dock somewhere along the coast of Brittany to deliver supplies for the scholars of Rennes in the Kingdom of the Franks.	「Frastrada」號會停靠布列塔尼沿岸某處，為法蘭克王國勒恩的學者們運送補給。
The Captain of the "Remus" seeks to reach Rome, but will stop in two Muslim-held ports, Malaga and Tunis.	「Remus」號的船長意欲抵達羅馬，但途中會停靠穆斯林治下的馬拉加與突尼斯兩港。
The "Athene" sails for Thessalonica, seeking also to trade in Malaga and Tunis.	「Athene」號駛往帖撒羅尼迦，同樣打算在馬拉加與突尼斯進行貿易。
Aye, 'tis fair seas for sailing at this time of year.	正是，這個時節海象宜人，適合航行。
I be guarding this gangplank, m'lud, while the Captain is ashore.	小人在此看守這條跳板，吾王，船長此刻正在岸上。
There will be only enough room for you and your mule, m'lud.  I will see that your horse is delivered safely to Camelot, as I did for Sir Galahad when he departed from here some months ago.	船上只夠容納吾王與您的騾子。小人會確保您的坐騎安全送回肯萊特，正如數月前葛拉漢爵士自此地啟程時，小人為他所做的一樣。
If that suits you, m'lud, you may book passage with me.	若這安排合吾王之意，便可向小人訂下船位。
Aye, there should be enough room for you as a passenger.   If you seek to travel, you may book passage through me, m'lud.	正是，作為乘客，空間應是夠用的。吾王若有意遠行，可經由小人訂下船位。
I cannot book a passage for you yet, m'lud.  Return later and I may be able to help you.	小人此刻還無法為吾王訂下船位。請稍後再來，屆時或能為您效勞。
Aye, 'tis part of a ship, m'lud.	正是，這是船的一部分，吾王。
Sail?  Did you say sail?  A ship will not get far without one, m'lud.	帆？您說的是帆嗎？沒有帆，船是走不遠的，吾王。
There are five ships in the port ready to depart.  Their destinations are Dublin, Rennes, Rome, Thessalonica and Gaza.	港中有五艘船已備妥啟航，目的地分別是都柏林、勒恩、羅馬、帖撒羅尼迦與加薩。
Several ships are in port, but none will be ready to sail again for some days.	港中雖有幾艘船，但短期內都不會再啟航。
We have had some trouble at the docks.  Drunken brawls amongst the sailors, that sort of thing.	碼頭這邊出了些麻煩，水手們酗酒鬥毆，諸如此類的事。
The crews will be unfit to sail for days yet.	船員們這幾天都還不宜出海。
They be ashore in search of grog and women, m'lud.	他們上岸去找烈酒與女人了，吾王。
You cannot deny the sailors a bit of fun while they are in port, not after months at sea.	在港停留期間，總不能不讓水手們稍作享樂，畢竟他們才在海上熬了數月。
We have a number of foreign captains in port this day.  They are doing business with the port merchants.	今日港中有幾位外邦船長，他們正與港口商人洽談生意。
We do a fair business here, m'lud.  Mostly we trade our tin, furs and some weapons, and receive trade goods of many kinds.	此地生意還算興隆，吾王。我們多以錫、毛皮與一些兵器進行交易，換得各式各樣的貨品。
We commonly trade it to foreign lands, as m'lud surely knows.	我們常將它與外邦交易，這點吾王想必清楚。
It is just some honey and tin waiting to be loaded onto the proper ship.	這不過是些等著裝上該去的船的蜂蜜與錫。
The shore is green this time of year.	這個時節，岸邊一片翠綠。
Aye, there are Vikings around Dublin and Saracen pirates in the Mediterranean.  They are the scourge of honest merchants, m'lord.	正是，都柏林一帶有維京人，地中海則有撒拉遜海盜，他們是誠實商人的禍害，吾王。
Aye aye, an eye for an eye, say I.	正是正是，以眼還眼，小人向來這麼說。
Awrr, they are the heathen worshippers of a foreign god, but they rule most of the Mediterranean now, so we must deal with them.	唉，他們是信奉外邦異神的異教徒，但如今地中海大半為其所據，我們也只得與之往來。
Fearing? I be afeared of nothing but the sea, m'lud.	害怕？小人這輩子除了大海，什麼都不怕，吾王。
My hearing? Aye, the roar of sea and wind has deafened me a trifle.	耳朵？正是，海浪與風聲的咆哮，把小人的耳朵震得有些背了。
Pray pardon me, m'lud, but I cannot accept your fare now, until I have a ship on which to book you a passage.  I beg you to return later.	還請吾王見諒，小人此刻手邊尚無可訂位的船隻，暫不能收下船費。懇請您稍後再來。
For this transaction, it would be better to dismount.	辦理此事，最好先下馬。
Move closer to the Harbourmaster.	靠近港務司一些。
Beg pardon, m'lud, but I did not hear you ask for a port of call yet.	請恕小人失禮，吾王，方才未曾聽見您說要去哪個港口。
If you wish. I am sure the Harbourmaster can help you with that.	若您有意，港務司想必能幫上忙。
Pardon, m'lud, but that is not a port and no ship sails there.	恕小人直言，吾王，那並非港口，沒有船隻駛往該處。
Beggin' m'lud's pardon, but I be a trifle hard of hearing. I did not hear where you wished to go.	請吾王恕罪，小人耳朵有些背，方才沒聽清您想去哪裡。
Eh? Never heard of it.  'Tis some piddling little foreign rathole, I suppose.	嗯？沒聽過這地方。想必是哪個不入流的外邦小地方吧。
But m'lud has paid nothing that I might refund.	但吾王並未付過分毫，小人也就無從退還。
As you command, m'lud.  I shall return what you have given me.	遵命，吾王。小人這便將您所付的奉還。
Others might be surprised to see you here, m'lud, but not I.  Ever since Sir Galahad sailed from here and did not return, I felt another would follow in his steps.	旁人見您在此，或許會感到訝異，吾王，但小人不會。自葛拉漢爵士自此啟航、一去未歸之後，小人便料想會有人步上他的後塵。
Though little did I suspect it would be our most noble knight and King himself.	只是小人萬萬沒料到，這人竟會是我們最尊貴的騎士、我們的王親自前來。
If you wish to book passage upon one of them, m'lud, I will take your fare myself, for by your own law every man--even a king--must pay his way.	吾王若欲訂下其中一艘的船位，小人自當親自收取船費——依您自己所定的律法，人人皆須自付旅費，即便是王也不例外。
If you have come to follow Galahad, m'lud, you have come at a bad time.  Several ships are in port, but none will be ready to sail again for some days.  I suggest you return later.	吾王若是為了追尋葛拉漢而來，此刻時機不巧。港中雖有幾艘船，但短期內都不會再啟航。小人建議您稍後再來。
Ah, m'lud, your return is most timely.  I have five ships leaving port.  They are sailing for Dublin, Rennes, Rome, Thessalonica and Gaza.	啊，吾王，您回來得正是時候。小人這裡有五艘船即將啟航，分別駛往都柏林、勒恩、羅馬、帖撒羅尼迦與加薩。
Would you care to book passage upon one of them? By your own law every man--even a king--must pay his way.   I would be pleased to answer any question you may ask about them.	您可願訂下其中一艘的船位？依您自己所定的律法，人人皆須自付旅費，即便是王也不例外。您若有任何疑問，小人樂意一一為您解答。
Greetings, m'lud.  I fear you have returned too soon.  We have had some trouble at the docks.  Drunken brawls amongst the sailors, that sort of thing.	見過吾王。恐怕您回來得太早了些。碼頭這邊出了些麻煩，水手們酗酒鬥毆，諸如此類的事。
The crews will be unfit to sail for days yet.  You had best return later.	船員們這幾天都還不宜出海，您最好稍後再來。
Beggin' m'lud's pardon, but only coin may be collected for fare.	請吾王恕罪，船費只收錢幣。
Sorry, m'lud, it is already sold.	抱歉，吾王，這東西已經賣出去了。
I have five ships bound for different parts of the world on which you might book passage.  They sail for Dublin, Rennes, Rome, Thessalonica and Gaza.	小人這裡有五艘駛向世界各地的船，供您訂位。它們分別前往都柏林、勒恩、羅馬、帖撒羅尼迦與加薩。
If you wish to book passage on one of them, m'lud, I will be most happy to tell you the fare for each.	吾王若欲訂下其中一艘的船位，小人樂意一一告知各船的船費。
Beggin' m'lud's pardon, but I may accept only coin as the proper fare.	請吾王恕罪，船費只能以錢幣支付。
No need to part with it, m'lud.  There will be just enough room on the ship for it.	不必捨棄它，吾王，船上剛好夠容納。
I am not in the mule buying business, m'lud.	小人不做買騾子的生意，吾王。
Methinks the man is hard of hearing, Arthur.	依我看，這人耳朵有些背，亞瑟。
It would improper of you to break the seals on merchandise that does not belong to you.	拆封不屬於你的貨物，這是不妥當的。
Did you not hear, Arthur?  Galahad went to Jerusalem.	你沒聽見嗎，亞瑟？葛拉漢去了耶路撒冷。
If you want to know about ship destinations, booking passage or fares, you should ask the Harbourmaster about them.	若想知道船隻的目的地、如何訂位或船費，該去問港務司。
It is fairly calm, indicating light wind.	海面相當平靜，顯示風勢不大。
Beneath you is the dock.	你腳下便是碼頭。
Ask the Harbourmaster.	去問港務司。
It is fully loaded and ready to sail.	它已裝載完畢，隨時可以啟航。
It has not yet finished with loading and unloading of cargo and supplies.  But the Harbourmaster would know more than I about such things.	貨物與補給尚未裝卸完畢。不過這類事情，港務司會比我清楚。
A foreign ship is moored along one side of the dock.  Yonder portly fellow is the Harbourmaster, who has authority over all ships that enter and leave Southampton.   Some cargo has been off-loaded from the ship and awaits delivery.	碼頭一側停泊著一艘外國船。那邊那位體態豐腴的人便是港務司，凡出入南安普頓港的船隻都歸他管轄。船上已卸下一些貨物，正等候運送。
My hearing is excellent, thank you.	我的耳朵好得很，多謝關心。
It is Greek for "Kristi".	這是希臘語的「Kristi」。
Peter loves Christy and Christy loves Peter and that is all you need to know.	彼得愛克莉絲蒂，克莉絲蒂也愛彼得，你只需知道這些就夠了。
His whereabouts are yet unknown.	他的下落至今仍不明。
Aye, 'tis a mast.   It holds the sail.	正是，這是桅杆，用來張帆。
The gangplank is in place.  The ship must still be engaged in business.	跳板還架著，船想必仍在辦事。
It is furled atop the mast.	它捲收在桅杆頂端。
Perhaps the crews are having a final round of drinks at a local inn before departure.	船員們或許正在附近的客棧裡，趁啟航前再喝上最後一輪。
He will surely appear once the Harbourmaster decrees the ship is cleared to leave.	一旦港務司宣布船隻獲准啟航，他必定會現身。
The waves break on the shoreline of Southampton.	海浪拍打著南安普頓港的岸線。
Aye, a ship has many ropes.	正是，一艘船上有許多繩索。
Every ship has one.	每艘船都有一個。
'Tis not an uncommon practice among foreign seaman to paint an eye upon the prow so that the ship may better see where it is going.	外邦水手在船首畫上一隻眼睛，好讓船能看清前路，這並非罕見的習俗。
It is a typical merchant ship bringing foreign cargo to trade for British goods such as tin.	這是一艘典型的商船，載著外邦貨物，前來交換不列顛的錫等物產。
There is a small bit of shelter in the prow, but no cabins.  These ships are built for cargo, not comfort.	船首有一小塊遮蔽之處，但沒有艙房。這種船是為載貨而造，不是為了舒適。
The ship's stern has a rudder, as might be expected.	船尾一如預期，裝有舵。
It is, not surprisingly, the shoreline of Southampton.	不出所料，這正是南安普頓港的岸線。
The clouds do not look threatening and should not delay the ship from sailing.	這些雲看來並無威脅，應不至於耽誤船隻啟航。
The earthenware pots and jars might contain wax, oil, wine or honey.	這些陶罐與陶甕裡，或許裝著蠟、油、酒或蜂蜜。
The packets are wrapped in oil cloth and could be any number of common trade items:  spices, furs, cloth, ivory, amber, glass beads, pottery.	這些包裹以油布包紮，裡頭可能是各式各樣常見的貿易貨品：香料、毛皮、布匹、象牙、琥珀、玻璃珠、陶器。
There are many fish in the sea, Arthur, and seagulls to feast upon them.	海裡魚多得很，亞瑟，海鷗也樂得飽餐一頓。
The cargo on the dock consists of earthenware pots and jars and some wrapped packets.	碼頭上的貨物，是些陶罐、陶甕與幾包用布包紮的東西。
Since a goodly portion of your tax revenues come from shipping, I suppose it must be doing well enough.	既然您稅收有相當一部分來自航運，我想生意想必還算興隆。
